{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4705",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is implicated in the interaction with Ndufa10 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participate in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. This activity is then directly participated by Ndufa10, establishing a potential functional link between Metformin and Ndufa10. The high scores across the three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, suggesting that Metformin may influence Ndufa10 through a mechanism involving the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ndufa10 supports the idea that Metformin's interaction with Ndufa10 is mediated through this enzymatic activity, potentially affecting mitochondrial function or energy metabolism.",
